===Etymology 1===
{{ety|en|id=factual|:inh|enm:trewe|tree=1}}
From {{inh|en|enm|trewe}}, {{m|enm|true}}, from {{inh|en|ang|trēowe}}, {{m|ang|trīewe|t=faithful, true}}, from {{inh|en|gem-pro|*triwwiz|t=faithful, true}}, from pre-Germanic *''drewh₂yos'', from {{der|en|ine-pro|*drew-|*drewh₂-|t=firm, hard, true}}.
{{col-top|2|cog}}
Cognate with {{cog|stq|trjou|t=honest}}, {{cog|gsw|trüüw|t=loyal}}, {{cog|nl|trouw|t=loyal, true}}, {{cog|de|treu|t=loyal, true}}, {{cog|lb|trei|t=loyal}}, {{cog|da|tryg|t=safe, secure}}, {{cog|fo,is|tryggur|t=faithful, loyal; safe}}, {{cog|nb,nn,sv|trygg|t=safe, secure}}, {{cog|got|𐍄𐍂𐌹𐌲𐌲𐍅𐍃|t=true; faithful, loyal}}; also {{cog|ga|dearbh|t=sure}}, {{cog|prg|druwis||faith}}, {{cog|grc|δροόν||firm}}), extension of {{m|ine-pro|*dóru||tree}} (possibly also {{cog|sla-pro|*sъdorvъ||healthy}} from the same root). More at {{m|en|tree}}. For the semantic development, compare {{cog|la|robustus||tough}} from {{m|la|robur||red oak}}.
